   "resolution": "fix: Retain official key D, confirmed by the source image and Archimedes’ principle; no examiner comment is present. Repair the damaged extracted ratio and options. In build/work/mcq/overrides.json under qid 9702_w23_11_q14, set exactly these fields (preserve other fields): {\"stem\": \"An object of weight W is suspended from a newton meter. When the object is completely immersed in water, the newton meter reads P. When the object is completely immersed in oil, the newton meter reads Q. What is the ratio (density of oil)/(density of water)?\", \"options\": {\"A\": \"(W - P)/(Q - P)\", \"B\": \"(Q - P)/(W - P)\", \"C\": \"(W - P)/(W - Q)\", \"D\": \"(W - Q)/(W - P)\"}, \"answer\": \"D\", \"explanation\": \"In equilibrium, the newton meter reading plus the upthrust equals W. Hence the upthrust is W - P in water and W - Q in oil. By Archimedes’ principle, upthrust = density × g × V. The same object is fully submerged in both liquids, so g and V cancel: (density of oil)/(density of water) = (W - Q)/(W - P), option D. The image asks for oil divided by water; C is the reciprocal. A and B incorrectly use Q - P, the difference between the upthrusts, in place of one of the upthrusts.\"}"
